You have been provided specialized ChatAnalyst tooling for this job; use this tooling instead of general Workspace tooling like bash, python or ruby when reading conversation logs in Chat format. Resorting to using tools like read or bash over chat logs is considered a deviation justified by shortcomings of the ChatAnalyst tooling. Please report those if they can lead to tooling improvements.

The exported task family is 25 Scout tasks, all TSV outputs except the
two byte-exact `:chat` retrievals and one `:text` point read (see the
ChatAnalyst README for the full tables). Retrieval ladder: indexes first,
bodies last; every step between tasks passes ONLY paths and integer
indices — unescape a path before feeding it back into a task input.

- `chat_overview` — tree overview: one row per chat (messages, references,
  warnings); annotations chats/jobs/delegations. Start here.
- `job_overview` — jobs of the tree with their chat-typed result chats,
  dependency counts, live log counts.
- `chat_activity_clusters` — the DEFAULT temporal entry point: compact
  cluster index (no member lists); annotations clusters/inferences/
  unclustered. Never returns all inferences.
- `chat_activity_cluster` — members of ONE cluster (needs `cluster_id` from
  the index; same `max_gap_seconds`).
- `chat_inferences` — paginated tree-wide inference drill-down; optional
  `chat` filter narrows rows only.
- `chat_messages` — zero-based message index of ONE chat (role filter,
  pagination, `large` flag); never bodies.
- `chat_message` — byte-exact ONE message, addressed by Message id.
- `chat_range` — byte-exact persisted slice, inclusive `first`..`last`
  (cap 200); `first == last` fetches one message. THE evidence surface.
- `chat_references` — reference index of one chat: job_reference /
  delegation / import / continue / last; delegation rows name their
  `agent#conversation` target.
- `job_dependencies` / `job_dependencies_recursive` — declared direct
  edges (1-based order) and the cycle-safe closure (`max_depth`).
- `chat_role_counts` — message counts per chat and role.
- `chat_tool_calls` — tree-wide call index; filters tool/agent/
  conversation/chat/success + pagination; metadata only.
- `chat_tool_call` — ONE call's metadata row: status, reason, timestamps,
  argument/output character counts, output_message_id.
- `chat_tool_call_jobs` — one row per (call, referenced job) pair.
- `chat_tokens` — token SUMMARY (4 scope rows); chat_evidence and
  receipt_evidence overlap — never sum them.
- `chat_token_events` / `chat_token_evidence` — paginated deduplicated
  events and their aligned evidence rows.
- `chat_attribution` — root/delegated/unattributed token split.
- `chat_accounting` — per-chat accounting over the import closure
  (`scope` own/closure).
- Operational: `live_chats` (live file discovery), `chat_live_report`
  (running-state entries; separate from live_chats), `inbox_state`
  (index-only), `inbox_note` (one note body), `post_inbox_advice` (post
  advice; the reserved `abort` name is rejected).

TSV read discipline: pagination and scope ride the `#: :page=...`-
style annotation line (read them through the TSV options, not the rows);
keys and path cells carry ESCAPED paths — unescape before reuse; parse a
Message id on the FIRST `#` (path part, then the zero-based index);
booleans are the strings `true`/`false`; `\N` is null and `""` is the
empty string; multi-value cells are `|`-joined and `|`-free.

Worked chain (a failed tool call): `chat_overview` ->
`chat_activity_clusters` -> `chat_inferences` (chat filter, page) ->
`chat_tool_calls` (success=false) -> `chat_tool_call` (metadata row) ->
`chat_range` on the output message id. Only paths and indices pass
between steps; no digests are memorized.

Cell-content rule: TSV cells never carry message bodies, reasoning text,
tool argument/output content or exception text — only identifiers, paths,
enumerations, counts, sizes and booleans. Establish message evidence
through `chat_range` (or `chat_message`), never by reading the raw chat
file with general tooling when the task surface reaches it.

Operational guidance: keep LIVE discovery (`live_chats`,
`chat_live_report`) separate from settled provenance analysis; read note
bodies with `inbox_note`, never through the index; post advice with
`post_inbox_advice` only when you intend to steer a running inference
(every safeguard is enforced; `abort` is reserved). `chat_tokens` answers
"what did tokens cost" over evidence scopes; `chat_accounting` answers
"what did each chat import and spend" — different questions.

Notes: message indices are zero-based and ranges are inclusive;
`characters` counts parsed message content, never file bytes; embedded
`meta` receipts are evidence, not messages, so they never appear in
message indexes — they surface through the token tasks' evidence
locations. Every chat path in a cell or key is one canonical spelling
(escaped); unescaped it feeds back into any task. `:chat` outputs carry
their addressing in the persisted job inputs, not in the output text.
Retired task names (chat_timeline, message_index, message_content,
extract_chat_range, chat_report) raise TaskNotFound; the README's
retirement sections and `var/baselines/` record what replaced them.

